{
  "schema": 1,
  "meta": {
    "name": "Growl (FM)",
    "description": "A wavetable phase-modulated by a silent sine at 1:1, with a looping quarter-note MSEG moving the PM index, the wavetable position, the modulator's pitch, a band-pass and a formant (a towards o), then asymmetric distortion, a band-pass, a formant and a sine fold, OTT and an EQ (low cut 150 Hz, a bell at 400 Hz). The mid-range vowel-like growl of report 04 (S4).",
    "tags": [
      "bass",
      "growl",
      "fm"
    ]
  },
